  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f: X \\rightarrow X$ be such that $f[f(x)]=x,$ for all\r\n$x \\in X$ and $X \\subseteq R,$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kIBKV",
      "text": "$f$ is one-to-one",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lhPTx",
      "text": "$f$ is onto",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JRSgD",
      "text": "$f$ is one-to-one but not onto",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iuI3I",
      "text": "$f$ is onto but not one-to-one",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $f(f(x)]=x$ \r\nNow, $\\quad f^{-1}(x)=f(x)$\r\nLe. $f(x)$ is bijective. \r\nHence, $f(x)$ has to be one-one and onto.",
    "image": null
  },
